# Raw material from the client, before it has been processed.
#
# public/images/Product2/ is the WhatsApp dump he sent on 2 September: 5 photos
# and 32 videos, 205MB. It must never be committed, for two separate reasons.
#
# Git history is permanent. 205MB added once stays in every clone forever, even
# after a later commit deletes it, and Cloudflare re-downloads the whole repo
# on every build.
#
# And it is inside public/, which means anything left there is PUBLISHED. The
# whole folder would be downloadable from the live site — including a picture
# carrying a GPS Map Camera stamp with a customer's address and coordinates on
# it. Nobody would ever see it on a page, and it would be served all the same.
#
# What ships is what came out of it: the stills in images/products/ and
# images/projects/, and the compressed loops in images/clips/. Keep this folder
# somewhere outside the project — it is the negative, not the print.
public/images/Product2/

# Client-facing deliverables — videos, quotations, exports.
# Kept out of git deliberately: they are outputs, not source, and git history
# is permanent. A re-recorded 11MB walkthrough would add 11MB to the repo
# forever, and Cloudflare re-downloads the whole repo on every build.
docs/*.mp4
docs/*.webm
docs/*.pdf
docs/*.docx

npm-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
.vercel
.idea/
.vscode/*
!.vscode/extensions.json
